  "body": "## What changed\n\nUnnamed generation checks freshness as it reaches each operation in program order.\nIt regenerates downstream operations made stale by an earlier generation in the same call.\nNamed generation keeps its existing behavior.\nThe MCP description explains the order and refusal behavior.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe loop filtered its targets using statuses captured before generation started.\nIt missed operations that became stale during the call.\n\n## Tests\n\n`unnamed_generate_rechecks_downstream_freshness_in_program_order` fails before the fix and passes after it.\nIt checks every operation after one call, the generated order, and the empty second call.\nRestoring upstream's `api.rs` makes this pin fail again.\nRestoring the fix makes both pins pass.\n`named_generate_always_regenerates_only_the_named_operation` passes.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes all 17 steps.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\nValidation disabled the stalled compile-cache wrapper.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe diff contains no changed `.nc` or `.cl` files.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe GUI was not run.\nInspection confirms its separate `RegenerateAll` command already uses rounds.\nNo CNC hardware was exercised.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2253 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt changes `v_load`, `holds_post`, and `op_view` in `script/api.rs`.\nThis fix changes `v_generate`.\nPRs #2149, #2134, and #2092 touch different tool entries in `mcp/tools.rs`.\nEach touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nThis fix changes only the `generate` description in that table.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: Generate without a name now regenerates operations made stale by earlier generations in the same call.\n\nFixes #2439\n",
